       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than double the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults, and some protocols cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual 1,000 mg maximum. A dose like this risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n- **3000 mg/day total**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 3000 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest adding a note with the clinical rationale."
